<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani cotton output reaches 475,200 bales.</title>
<headline>Pakistani cotton output reaches 475,200 bales.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's state-run Cotton Export Corporation said on Monday that cotton output in 1996/97 (July-June) had reached a provisional 475,200 375-lb bales by September 19, up from 245,400 in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>It said mills had bought 417,500 bales, up from 218,500 in the same period of 1995/96. Ginneries had stocks of 57,700 unsold bales, compared to 26,900 a year ago.</p>
<p>Agriculture authorities said on Sunday they expected the crop to exceed 11 million bales this year despite a white fly pest attack. This would surpass the official target of 10 million. Output was 9.96 million bales last year.</p>
<p>-- Ovais Subhani 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
